:''This article is about the enemy. For the Cat Unit, see [[E. Honda (Uber Rare Cat)]].''
'''E. Honda''' is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = E. Honda
|image = E 528.png
|first appearance = [[Pride & Passion (Normal)]]
|money drop = 950¢ - 3,950¢
}}

==Enemy==
This sumo wrestler is not as strong as he seems. Sure he has high health being at 500,000, but his attack power is rather low, not even reaching 6,000. His standing range is also something to be considered, being at a measly 100, however, take note of his [[Omni Strike]] range as it is able to reach up to 300 meaning that he is able to outrange many close ranged attackers. He also has a 100% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] all Cat Units. It is good to note that he is not Floating despite appearances.

==Strategy==
Units such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], the [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|crazed]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|counterparts]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and more can hit E. Honda from a safe distance. Anything that is [[Immune to Knockback|Immune to knockback]], especially [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]], should be avoided, as this doesn't allow them to be pushed from a safe range away from E. Honda and will be continuously hit by his attacks. Any unit that can do damage in a singular blow is more effective, as that will trigger less of his knockbacks, and thus less of his attacks.

